Description: Make the librsvg2-bin man-page install path nodoc-proof
 `debian/librsvg2-bin.install` lists `usr/share/man` (rsvg-convert(1)).
 Under `DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc` the upstream build does not generate
 man pages, `usr/share/man` is absent from `debian/tmp/`, and
 `dh_install` (compat 13 = --fail-missing) aborts.
 .
 An earlier revision of this patch instead DROPPED the `usr/share/man`
 line from `debian/librsvg2-bin.install`.  That traded one failure
 mode for its mirror image: with docs enabled (Athena's current
 config — `[Source]` BuildOptions/BuildProfiles emptied by the
 operator, 2026-07), the built rsvg-convert.1 lands in debian/tmp but
 nothing installs it, and `dh_missing` aborts the build:
 .
   dh_missing: warning: usr/share/man/man1/rsvg-convert.1 exists in
   debian/tmp but is not installed to anywhere
   dh_missing: error: missing files, aborting
 .
 This revision takes the dynamic-gate route the earlier header already
 prescribed: keep the stock install list and pre-create
 `debian/tmp/usr/share/man` in `override_dh_install` before dh_install
 runs.  Docs-enabled builds are byte-identical to stock (the mkdir is
 a no-op; the man page ships in librsvg2-bin as Debian intends);
 nodoc builds get an empty directory, which dh_install copies without
 complaint instead of failing on a missing source path.  Works in
 both modes; no dh_missing regression in either.
 .
 Originally surfaced during GROUPS-01 phase 3 gnome build 2026-05-14
 (nodoc direction); re-surfaced 2026-07-06 full-testsuite run (docs
 direction, dh_missing).
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-07-06
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@
 	find debian/tmp -name '*.a' -print -delete
 	find debian/tmp -name '*.la' -print -delete
 	rm -f debian/tmp/usr/bin/rsvg-view-3
+	mkdir -p debian/tmp/usr/share/man
 	dh_install
 	sed -e "s/#MULTIARCH#/$(DEB_HOST_MULTIARCH)/g" debian/librsvg2-common.postinst.in > \
 		debian/librsvg2-common.postinst
